    "title": "File timestamp modified (timestomp)",
    "desc": "A file's timestamp was set by hand - touch with an explicit time (-t / -d / --date) or copied from another file (-r / --reference). Backdating a dropped file so it blends with its neighbours, or matching it to a system binary's time, is anti-forensics (MITRE T1070.006): it defeats a timeline built on mtime/atime. A plain `touch` that just creates a file or bumps it to now is not matched.",
